So, been frustrated with trying to ascend a Knight on NAO (I had one get
foiled on the Astral *sigh*), I decided to go Tourist. Beginning went
poorly, as my pet got lunched on level 6, but I was able to..very
carefully...dart and elbereth my way to minetown, where there was another
dog to throw tripe to. After cleaning out minetown, I headed to Sokoban
where my pet (whom I'd grown tired of at this point) decided to attack one
of the giant mimics on the top floor, and that solved my annoying pet
problem.

Bag of Holding in hand, I went down below Minetown where I hit my first
stroke of good luck, a pretty decent bones file...+2 GDSM, and a magic
lamp, among some other sundry items. With magic resistance in hand, one of
the gnomes at mine's end was kind enough to donate speed boots, and I
picked up the luckstone and headed down the dungeon.

A random floor spawn gave a helm of brilliance, and then another bones file
gave a whole bunch of niceness. Magicbane (wizard char), trollsbane, a
second BoH, amulet of relfection, bunch of spellbooks, giant pile of
scrolls/wands, basically a bunch of nice mid-game stash stuff.

Ludios had a blue and a black dragon, giving me my last two intrinsics, and
one of the soldiers had some +3 leather gloves. With all that I'd
recovered, I was fully intrinisic'd, had nearly every important item
identified, magic resistance, good weapons, -34 AC with armor and priest
protection, and I went down and  cleared out the quest level...the master
of thieves was a decided wimp.

So, I headed back to my stash to go on an identifying spree for the couple
of new unknowns I'd found, and (since one of the spellbooks I'd located was
identify), to see the charges on my wands and pair of magic markers so I
could look into making use of my first ever PYEC.

So I'm sitting there on my burnt Elbereth'd stash square casting identify
on stuff, and hoping to get an identify-all and flush out a whole bunch of
stuff at once, I had taken off all my armor and dropped it and all the
already identified stuff on the ground to fit the most wands in inventory,
when a couple of monsters come wandering into my stash room. One was a
mummy, the other....was a cockatrice.

I pick up my weapons and kill them both, and then I get the idea to throw a
sacrifice onto the altar, cause my luck was only +5 or so, so I hop over to
pick up the corpse...with my gloves sitting on the ground.

*sigh*

Absent such rank stupidity, that one was going all the way. I hadn't even
hit the castle level yet, so I could have used the castle wand to wish up
some SDSM and a CoMR to free up the amulet slot for a lifesaving (which I
had one of sitting in my bag).

On the plus side, if that left a bones file behind, SOMEONE is going to be
